{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HQgV2YAMjjBkLMkmWtkkro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the information I need. Let me update Item 10 to IN_PROGRESS and then implement the GlobalExceptionHandler.\n\nThe GlobalExceptionHandler needs to:\n1. Be in `com.example.legacy.controller` package with @ControllerAdvice\n2. Handle:\n   - `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 with fieldErrors populated from BindingResult\n   - `NotFoundException` → 404\n   - `DuplicateEmailException` → 409\n   - `BadRequestException` → 400\n   - Generic `Exception` → 500\n3. All responses use `ErrorResponse` DTO with ISO 8601 timestamp\n\n\n4. Return JSON format\n\nI'm creating the exception handler class with methods for each exception type. Looking at the plan again, I notice Item 16 is actually the EmployeeController test, not the GlobalExceptionHandler test, so I'll need to create a separate test for this handler. I see the inconsistency now — the plan says GlobalExceptionHandler tests are covered by Item 16, but Item 16 is actually the EmployeeController. Since I need to follow the \"write tests alongside implementation\" rule and hit that 70% test code target, I should create the GlobalExceptionHandler with its own unit test using MockMvc, probably with a minimal test controller to avoid needing a full application context in Spring 4.3.\n\nWriting GlobalExceptionHandler implementation... I'm setting up a formatter for ISO timestamps and creating an exception handler that processes validation errors by extracting field-level errors and building a structured response.\n\nNow I'm adding handlers for other common exceptions—not found errors return 404, duplicate email attempts return 409 conflict status—each constructing an error response with the appropriate HTTP status code and timestamp.\n\nI should also add a catch-all handler for any unexpected exceptions that bubble up, returning a generic 500 internal server error. Let me verify the Java version supports the datetime utilities I'm using—Java 8 has LocalDateTime and DateTimeFormatter, so that's compatible.\n\nNow I'm setting up the test infrastructure with MockMvc to verify these exception handlers work correctly across different error scenarios. Writing test cases... Finishing the timestamp assertion, then moving on to test the generic exception handler. For the MethodArgumentNotValidException test, I'll need a controller endpoint that accepts a validated request body—I can create a test endpoint that takes a @Valid @RequestBody and POST invalid data to trigger the validation error.\n\nThe tricky part is that standalone MockMvc doesn't automatically configure validation the same way a full Spring context does. I need to check whether `StandaloneMockMvcBuilder` sets up a default validator or if I need to explicitly configure one.\n\nActually, it looks like Spring MVC does register a default validator automatically when the validation library is on the classpath, so I should be able to test this directly. I'll create a test endpoint that accepts a `@Valid` request body and send it invalid data to trigger the `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler.\n\nWriting the test endpoint and validation test...\n\nNow I need to verify what testing dependencies are available in the pom.xml to make sure I have everything I need for the assertions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1754,"cache_read_input_tokens":43557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1754},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f871528-f57d-4a1c-ae61-fad4f2fa2895","uuid":"528f9283-64ea-4924-916a-bd55f12560c2"}
